module tecs.internal.framepacket

--[[
Extraction for the Rust-owned GPU lane.

One host-endian packet crosses the managed ABI per completed frame. Nupp owns
world queries, camera selection, depth, draw ordering, material numbering, and
the render graph's declaration; Rust validates the packet and owns targets,
pipelines, culling, compaction, submission, and presentation. Image pixels
never ride in a packet. They cross once through the residency commands
`tecs.gfx.images` queues, so a frame carries only the id a batch binds.

# Packet version 7

Every field is little or big endian to match the host, every integer is
unsigned, and every real is a 32-bit float. Offsets are in bytes from the start
of the packet.

## Header, 128 bytes

| Offset | Type  | Field             | Contract                                             |
| ------ | ----- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| 0      | `u32` | `magic`           | `0x54454353`, and nothing else is a Tecs packet.      |
| 4      | `u32` | `version`         | `7`. A reader rejects every other value.              |
| 8      | `u32` | `headerSize`      | `128`. The graph section starts after it.             |
| 12     | `u32` | `flags`           | Bits 0/1 enable shadows/bloom; bits 2/3 retain/patch instances.           |
| 16     | `u32` | `graphRevision`   | A reader rebuilds its graph when this changes.        |
| 20     | `u32` | `graphBytes`      | Byte length of the graph section.                     |
| 24     | `u32` | `batchStride`     | `20`.                                                 |
| 28     | `u32` | `batchCount`      | Zero only when `instanceCount` is zero.               |
| 32     | `u32` | `instanceStride`  | `80`.                                                 |
| 36     | `u32` | `instanceCount`   | Total resident instance count, including unchanged instances.            |
| 40     | `f32` | `targetWidth`     | Render target width in pixels, greater than zero.     |
| 44     | `f32` | `targetHeight`    | Render target height in pixels, greater than zero.    |
| 48     | `f32` | `cameraX`         | View center x in world units.                         |
| 52     | `f32` | `cameraY`         | View center y in world units, increasing downward.    |
| 56     | `f32` | `cameraZoom`      | Greater than zero.                                    |
| 60     | `f32` | `cameraRotation`  | Radians, turning the scene counter-clockwise.         |
| 64     | `u32` | `lightStride`     | `32`.                                                 |
| 68     | `u32` | `lightCount`      | At most 256, the ceiling one frame resolves.          |
| 72     | `u32` | `casterCount`     | Instances carrying a cast flag, which sizes the list. |
| 76     | `u32` | sceneRevision     | Resident generation; zero for an independent snapshot.                                                 |
| 80     | `f32` | `ambientR`        | Ambient red, at or above zero.                        |
| 84     | `f32` | `ambientG`        | Ambient green.                                        |
| 88     | `f32` | `ambientB`        | Ambient blue.                                         |
| 92     | `f32` | `shadowSteps`     | March samples at full attenuation, four or more.      |
| 96     | `f32` | `shadowHeight`    | World height a caster at height one stands.           |
| 100    | `f32` | `shadowMargin`    | World units outside the view a caster is kept.        |
| 104    | `f32` | `dropOpacity`     | Drop-shadow darkness at full weight, zero to one.     |
| 108    | `f32` | `dropLength`      | Longest a drop shadow may be, in world units.         |
| 112    | `f32` | `bloomThreshold`  | Brightness a pixel passes to be extracted.            |
| 116    | `f32` | `bloomKnee`       | Width of the threshold's soft knee, above zero.       |
| 120    | `f32` | `bloomIntensity`  | Scales the blurred contribution.                      |
| 124    | `u32` | `tileUpdates`     | Number of compact grid updates after the lights.                                                 |

The shadow and bloom fields are written whether or not their flag is set, so a
backend reads one layout and the flag alone decides. A reader validates them
only when the flag they belong to is set.

## Graph section, `graphBytes` bytes at offset 128

The pass and target declaration, as `tecs.gpu.passes.section` encodes it. It
rides in every packet rather than being sent once, so a backend that lost its
device, its surface, or its whole graphics object rebuilds from the next frame
instead of holding state the sender cannot see. `graphRevision` is what keeps
that cheap: a reader parses the section only when the revision differs from the
one it built its graph from.

## Light table, `lightCount` entries of 32 bytes after the graph section

| Offset | Type  | Field       | Contract                                        |
| ------ | ----- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| 0      | `f32` | `x`         | World x of the light.                           |
| 4      | `f32` | `y`         | World y, increasing downward.                   |
| 8      | `f32` | `height`    | Height above the surface plane in world units.  |
| 12     | `f32` | `radius`    | Reach in world units, greater than zero.        |
| 16     | `f32` | `r`         | Red.                                            |
| 20     | `f32` | `g`         | Green.                                          |
| 24     | `f32` | `b`         | Blue.                                           |
| 28     | `f32` | `intensity` | Scales the contribution, at or above zero.      |

Lights are ordered by ascending entity id, so the same scene bins and casts the
same way every frame however the archetypes are laid out. A world holding more
than the ceiling keeps the lowest ids and drops the rest.

## Compact tile grids

After the lights, `tileUpdates` records each carry a `u32` slot and 1,072 bytes:
twelve floats (tile width, height, atlas columns, spacing, margin, cell width,
cell height, offset x, offset y, atlas width, atlas height, zero), then 256
packed `u32` tile IDs. Full frames provide slots zero through count minus one;
deltas update existing slots; retained frames provide none.

Instance flag bit 4 selects a chunk. Its position/scale are the top-left chunk
pose, `u0` selects its grid slot, and `v0` is a conservative world-space culling
radius. Batches never mix chunks and ordinary quads. The GPU chooses 1,536
vertices per chunk instance or six per quad, including the shadow lane.

## Retained and partial frames

This is the old SpriteFramePacket dirty-range seam adapted to the managed ABI:
persistent instance storage and dirty ranges cross in place of a full snapshot.
A full frame carries the batch table and all instances. A retained frame (bit 2)
ends after the lights and names the receiver's already-validated scene revision;
it carries no batch or instance bytes. A delta frame (bit 3) also omits the batch
table, then carries a base revision, a range count (1 to 64), and that many
`u32 offset, u32 size` pairs followed by their bytes. Ranges are sorted,
nonoverlapping and aligned to whole instances. The header names the new revision.

A delta preserves the instance count, batch layout and caster count. Relayouts
send a full frame. The receiver validates every changed instance and rejects
unknown generations, malformed ranges, invalid material IDs and mismatched lanes.
The host reports its resident generation on the next call; zero requests a full
refresh after graphics reconstruction. `Extractor.packet` continues to return
an independent complete snapshot. Neither dirty-bit clearing nor a skipped
extraction loses a write: run comparisons use monotonic counters.

## Batch table, `batchCount` entries of 20 bytes after the tile grid updates (full frames)

| Offset | Type  | Field           | Contract                                                |
| ------ | ----- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| 0      | `u32` | `image`         | A `tecs.gfx.images` id, or `0` for the white fallback.   |
| 4      | `u32` | `sampler`       | Below `tecs.gfx.images.SAMPLER_COUNT`.                   |
| 8      | `u32` | `lane`          | `0` opaque, `1` blended.                                 |
| 12     | `u32` | `firstInstance` | Zero-based index of the batch's first instance.          |
| 16     | `u32` | `instanceCount` | At least one.                                            |

Batches partition the instances exactly: the first starts at zero, each one
starts where the previous ended, and their counts sum to `instanceCount`. They
are runs in draw order rather than a grouping, because the scene is drawn back
to front and reordering by image would reorder the picture.

A run breaks on the lane as well as on the image and the sampler, so every
batch belongs to one lane. That is what lets a backend cull and compact the
instances and still draw a batch: compaction preserves packet order, so the
survivors of a single-lane batch are a contiguous run of that lane's visible
list and one indirect draw covers them.

## Instances, `instanceCount` entries of 80 bytes after the batch table (full frames)

| Offset | Type  | Field      | Contract                                                     |
| ------ | ----- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 0      | `f32` | `x`        | Center x in world units.                                      |
| 4      | `f32` | `y`        | Center y in world units.                                      |
| 8      | `f32` | `rotation` | Radians, turning the quad clockwise on screen.                |
| 12     | `f32` | `depth`    | Zero nearest to one farthest, from `tecs.gfx.layers.depthOf`. |
| 16     | `f32` | `scaleX`   | Full width in world units, not a half extent.                 |
| 20     | `f32` | `scaleY`   | Full height in world units.                                   |
| 24     | `f32` | `param`    | The material's own scalar, zero to one.                       |
| 28     | `f32` | `castHeight` | Caster height, zero to one of the shadow height. Zero otherwise. |
| 32     | `f32` | `u0`       | Left edge of the sampled region.                              |
| 36     | `f32` | `v0`       | Top edge of the sampled region.                               |
| 40     | `f32` | `u1`       | Right edge of the sampled region.                             |
| 44     | `f32` | `v1`       | Bottom edge of the sampled region.                            |
| 48     | `f32` | `r`        | Red, multiplied into the sampled color.                       |
| 52     | `f32` | `g`        | Green.                                                        |
| 56     | `f32` | `b`        | Blue.                                                         |
| 60     | `f32` | `a`        | Alpha, multiplied into the sampled alpha.                     |
| 64     | `u32` | `material` | A `tecs.gpu.materials` id, below the build's material count.  |
| 68     | `u32` | `flags`    | Bit 0 marks the blended lane and equals the batch's; bit 1 an occluder; bit 2 a drop-shadow caster; bit 3 enables clipping; bit 4 selects a tile grid. |
| 72     | `u32` | `clipMin` | Left in low 16 bits, top in high 16 bits; zero without bit 3.                                                         |
| 76     | `u32` | `clipMax` | Right in low 16 bits, bottom in high 16 bits; zero without bit 3.                                                         |

Bits 1 and 2 are exclusive of each other and neither is ever set with bit 0. An
entity carrying both `Occluder2D` and `DropShadow2D` is an occluder, because
dropping that half would silently unblock a light, and a blended entity casts
nothing at all: it never reaches the G-buffer, so a hard silhouette of it would
be a lie.

The four sixteen-byte groups and trailing words are what a backend binds as a storage buffer, so
the layout is a `vec4` quadruple followed by four words rather than the field
order a reader would pick.

Instances run in draw order: farthest depth first, and entity id ascending
between equal depths. A backend draws them in that order and the later one
covers the earlier, which is what makes the order deterministic between runs
without a tie-breaker of its own.

Every real in the packet is finite. A backend rejects a packet whose length
does not match its declared counts, whose strides differ from the constants
above, whose batches do not partition its instances, whose instance lane
disagrees with its batch's, or whose material id its dispatch does not carry.
]]

local archetype = require("tecs.internal.archetype")
local dirtyranges = require("tecs.internal.dirtyranges")
local images = require("tecs.gfx.images")
local layers = require("tecs.gfx.layers")
local clips = require("tecs.gfx.clips")
local lighting = require("tecs.gfx.lighting")
local materials = require("tecs.gpu.materials")
local passes = require("tecs.gpu.passes")
local query = require("tecs.internal.query")
local tilechunk = require("tecs.internal.tilechunk")
local cameraselection = require("tecs.internal.cameraselection")
local rendercomponents = require("tecs.internal.rendercomponents")
local world = require("tecs.internal.world")
local zone = require("nupp.profile.zone")
local array = require("nupp.mem.array")
local ffi = require("ffi")

--- Identifies a Tecs frame packet, and is a compatibility surface.
export const MAGIC: uint32 = 0x54454353

--- The packet layout this module writes.
export const VERSION: uint32 = 7

--- The byte length of the packet header.
export const HEADER_SIZE: uint32 = 128

--- The byte length of one batch table entry.
export const BATCH_STRIDE: uint32 = 20

--- The byte length of one instance.
export const INSTANCE_STRIDE: uint32 = 80

--- The byte length of one light table entry.
export const LIGHT_STRIDE: uint32 = 32

--- Names the lane that rasterizes into the G-buffer.
---
--- The lane numbering is a compatibility surface shared with the backend's
--- compaction, which fills one lane per dispatch.
export const LANE_OPAQUE: integer = 0

--- Names the lane the forward pass blends over the composited image.
export const LANE_BLEND: integer = 1

--- Marks an instance as belonging to the blended lane.
export const FLAG_BLENDED: integer = 1

--- Marks an instance as an occluder, whose silhouette enters the light mask.
export const FLAG_OCCLUDER: integer = 2

--- Marks an instance as a drop-shadow caster.
export const FLAG_DROP_SHADOW: integer = 4

--- Marks an instance with packed target-pixel clipping bounds.
export const FLAG_CLIPPED: integer = 8

--- Set in the header when the frame draws the shadow lane.
export const FRAME_SHADOWS: integer = 1

--- Set in the header when the frame draws the bloom chain.
export const FRAME_BLOOM: integer = 2

--- Reuses the receiver's validated resident instance generation.
export const FRAME_RETAINED: integer = 4

--- Carries dirty byte ranges over a validated resident generation.
export const FRAME_DELTA: integer = 8

const narrow = nupp.math.f32.narrow
const wrap = nupp.math.u32.wrap
const huge = math.huge

local function finite(value: number): boolean
    return value == value and value ~= huge and value ~= -huge
end

local record Run
    archetype: archetype.Archetype
    offset: integer
    length: integer
    structAt: integer
    valueAt: {integer}
    dirty: boolean
    seen: boolean
    screenSpace: boolean
    signature: string
    tileSlot: integer = 0
    tileBytes: string = ""
end

local record View
    width: integer
    height: integer
    x: number
    y: number
    zoom: number
    rotation: number
end

--- A world-bound renderer query with retained packed instances and dirty runs.
--- Clean runs preserve their packed bytes; the receiver supplies the generation
--- it has already validated and uploaded.
export record Extractor
    private world: world.World
    private drawCapacity: integer
    private lightCapacity: integer
    private drawables: query.Query
    private activeCameras: query.Query
    private cameras: query.Query
    private lights: query.Query
    private order: {integer}
    private entities: {integer}
    private depths: {number}
    private transforms: rendercomponents.Transform2D[?]
    private tints: rendercomponents.Tint[?]
    private clipIds: {integer}
    private imageIds: {integer}
    private samplers: {integer}
    private lanes: {integer}
    private chunkKinds: {boolean}
    private castFlags: {integer}
    private castHeights: {number}
    private materialIds: {integer}
    private params: {number}
    private u0: {number}
    private v0: {number}
    private u1: {number}
    private v1: {number}
    private cacheValid: boolean
    private sceneRevision: integer
    private runs: {[integer]: Run}
    private ranges: dirtyranges.Ranges
    private drawSlots: {integer}
    private relayout: boolean
    private batchDirty: boolean
    private rewritten: integer
    private cachedAlpha: number
    private cachedView: {number}
    private cachedLayers: integer
    private cachedClips: integer
    private cachedImages: integer
    private cachedMaterials: integer
    private cachedBatches: integer
    private cachedCasters: integer
    private cachedBatchBytes: string
    private screenSpace: boolean
    private instanceWords: array.Array<uint32>
    private orderChanged: boolean
    private rowCount: integer
    private sorted: integer
    private before: function(left: integer, right: integer): boolean
    private lightOrder: {integer}
    private lightEntities: {integer}
    private lightTransforms: rendercomponents.Transform2D[?]
    private lightValues: lighting.PointLight2D[?]
    private lightCount: integer
    private lightsSorted: integer
    private beforeLight: function(left: integer, right: integer): boolean

    --- Encodes a complete standalone snapshot, including every batch and instance.
    --- @param width the physical target width in pixels
    --- @param height the physical target height in pixels
    --- @return an independent packet that needs no receiver cache
    packet: function(exclusive self: Extractor, width: integer, height: integer): string

    --- Encodes a frame, omitting instances already resident at the receiver.
    frame: function(exclusive self: Extractor, width: integer, height: integer, residentRevision: integer): string
end

--- Creates an extractor and registers its queries with one world.
--- @param value the world whose renderable entities and cameras it reads
--- @return the extractor, which the caller keeps for the world's lifetime
export function new(exclusive value: world.World): Extractor
    local entities: {integer} = {}
    local depths: {number} = {}
    local before = function(left: integer, right: integer): boolean
        const leftDepth = depths[left]
        const rightDepth = depths[right]
        if leftDepth ~= rightDepth then
            -- Farthest first, so the nearer instance is drawn over it.
            return leftDepth > rightDepth
        end

        if entities[left] == entities[right] then
            return left < right
        end

        return entities[left] < entities[right]
    end
    local lightEntities: {integer} = {}
    -- Ascending entity id, so which lights survive the ceiling and which order
    -- a tile accumulates them in are the same for the same scene every frame.
    local beforeLight = function(left: integer, right: integer): boolean
        return lightEntities[left] < lightEntities[right]
    end

    return new Extractor(
        world = value,
        drawCapacity = 64,
        lightCapacity = 64,
        drawables = value:newQuery({
            exclude = {tecs.internal.components.Disabled},
            include = {
                rendercomponents.Transform2DComponent,
                rendercomponents.TintComponent,
                rendercomponents.Renderable2D,
            },
        }),
        activeCameras = value:newQuery({
            include = {rendercomponents.Camera2DComponent, rendercomponents.ActiveCamera},
        }),
        cameras = value:newQuery({include = {rendercomponents.Camera2DComponent}}),
        lights = value:newQuery({include = {rendercomponents.Transform2DComponent, lighting.PointLight2DComponent},}),
        order = {},
        entities = entities,
        depths = depths,
        transforms = carray(rendercomponents.Transform2D, 65),
        tints = carray(rendercomponents.Tint, 65),
        clipIds = {},
        imageIds = {},
        samplers = {},
        lanes = {},
        chunkKinds = {},
        castFlags = {},
        castHeights = {},
        materialIds = {},
        params = {},
        u0 = {},
        v0 = {},
        u1 = {},
        v1 = {},
        cacheValid = false,
        sceneRevision = 0,
        runs = {},
        ranges = dirtyranges.new(),
        drawSlots = {},
        relayout = true,
        batchDirty = true,
        rewritten = 0,
        cachedAlpha = -1,
        cachedView = {},
        cachedLayers = -1,
        cachedClips = -1,
        cachedImages = -1,
        cachedMaterials = -1,
        cachedBatches = 0,
        cachedCasters = 0,
        cachedBatchBytes = "",
        screenSpace = false,
        instanceWords = array.scalar(array.uint32, 256),
        orderChanged = true,
        rowCount = 0,
        sorted = 0,
        before = before,
        lightOrder = {},
        lightEntities = lightEntities,
        lightTransforms = carray(rendercomponents.Transform2D, 65),
        lightValues = carray(lighting.PointLight2D, 65),
        lightCount = 0,
        lightsSorted = 0,
        beforeLight = beforeLight
    )
end

--- Returns the view this frame projects through, as center, zoom, and rotation.
---
--- A world with no camera entity draws through a camera centered on the render
--- target at zoom one, which is the mapping that puts one world unit on one
--- target pixel with the origin at the top left corner.
--- @raises when the selected camera's zoom is not greater than zero, or when
---     any of its four values is not finite
local function view(borrows self: Extractor, width: number, height: number): number, number, number, number
    local camera = cameraselection.pick(self.activeCameras)
    if camera == nil then
        camera = cameraselection.pick(self.cameras)
    end
    if camera == nil then
        return width * 0.5, height * 0.5, 1.0, 0.0
    end
    if not (camera.zoom > 0.0) or not finite(camera.zoom) then
        error("framepacket: the active camera's zoom must be greater than zero", 3)
    end
    if not finite(camera.x) or not finite(camera.y) or not finite(camera.rotation) then
        error("framepacket: the active camera holds a value that is not finite", 3)
    end

    return camera.x, camera.y, camera.zoom, camera.rotation
end

--- Interpolates an extractor-owned native pose, never a borrowed simulation row.
local function presented(
    current: rendercomponents.Transform2D,
    previous: rendercomponents.PreviousTransform2D?,
    alpha: number
): rendercomponents.Transform2D
    if previous ~= nil then
        current.x = previous.x + (current.x - previous.x) * alpha
        current.y = previous.y + (current.y - previous.y) * alpha
        const angle = (current.rotation - previous.rotation + math.pi) % (2 * math.pi) - math.pi
        current.rotation = previous.rotation + angle * alpha
    end

    return current
end

-- Ordinary sprites retain archetype runs. A chunk owns one run so editing
-- a tile uploads only that chunk's retained instances when its size is stable.
local function sources(borrows self: Extractor): function(): (archetype.Archetype?, integer?, integer?, integer?)
    const nextArchetype = self.drawables:iter()
    local active: archetype.Archetype? = nil
    local length: integer = 0
    local row: integer = 0

    return function(): (archetype.Archetype?, integer?, integer?, integer?)
        if active ~= nil and row < length then
            row = row + 1
            return active, row, row, -active.entities[row]
        end
        const candidate, count = nextArchetype()
        if candidate == nil then
            return nil, nil, nil, nil
        end
        if archetype.has(candidate, tilechunk.TileChunkComponent) then
            active, length, row = candidate, assert(count), 1
            return candidate, 1, 1, -candidate.entities[1]
        end
        active = nil

        return candidate, 1, count, candidate.id
    end
end

--- Reads dirty archetype runs into the retained extraction arrays.
--- @raises when an entity selects a material id this build does not carry
local function collect(exclusive self: Extractor): nil
    local needed: integer = 0
    for _, run in pairs(self.runs) do
        needed = needed + run.length
    end
    if needed > self.drawCapacity then
        const capacity = math.max(needed, self.drawCapacity * 2)
        const transforms = carray(rendercomponents.Transform2D, capacity + 1)
        const tints = carray(rendercomponents.Tint, capacity + 1)
        ffi.copy(transforms, self.transforms, (self.rowCount + 1) * ffi.sizeof(rendercomponents.Transform2D))
        ffi.copy(tints, self.tints, (self.rowCount + 1) * ffi.sizeof(rendercomponents.Tint))
        self.transforms, self.tints, self.drawCapacity = transforms, tints, capacity
    end
    const entities = self.entities
    const depths = self.depths
    const transforms = self.transforms
    const tints = self.tints
    const imageIds = self.imageIds
    const samplers = self.samplers
    const lanes = self.lanes
    const castFlags = self.castFlags
    const castHeights = self.castHeights
    const materialIds = self.materialIds
    const params = self.params
    const u0 = self.u0
    const v0 = self.v0
    const u1 = self.u1
    const v1 = self.v1
    const materialCount = materials.count()
    local _, _, alpha = self.world:getFixedTiming()
    local rows: integer = 0
    local orderChanged = self.orderChanged
    -- Keep an interrupted collection invalid until a complete sort succeeds.
    self.orderChanged = true
    unsafe do
        for candidate, first, last, runKey in sources(self) do
            local active = candidate as archetype.Archetype
            const run = assert(self.runs[assert(runKey)])
            if not run.dirty then
                rows = rows + run.length
            else
                run.screenSpace = false
                local rowTransforms: rendercomponents.Transform2D[
                    ?
                ] = assert(active:get(rendercomponents.Transform2DComponent))
                const previous = active:get(rendercomponents.PreviousTransform2DComponent)
                local rowTints: rendercomponents.Tint[?] = assert(active:get(rendercomponents.TintComponent))
                local rowClips = active:get(clips.ClipComponent)
                local rowSprites = active:get(rendercomponents.SpriteComponent) as rendercomponents.Sprite[?]?
                local rowMaterials = active:get(materials.MaterialComponent) as materials.Material[?]?
                local rowOccluders = active:get(lighting.Occluder2DComponent) as lighting.Occluder2D[?]?
                local rowDropShadows = active:get(lighting.DropShadow2DComponent) as lighting.DropShadow2D[?]?
                const rowChunks = active:get(tilechunk.TileChunkComponent)
                for index = assert(first), assert(last) do
                    const chunk = rowChunks ~= nil and rowChunks[index] or nil
                    if chunk ~= nil and archetype.has(active, tilechunk.DirtyTileChunk) then
                        self.world:remove(active.entities[index], tilechunk.DirtyTileChunk)
                    end
                    do
                        if chunk ~= nil and run.length == 0 then
                            goto nextTile
                        end
                        rows = rows + 1
                        transforms[rows] = rowTransforms[index]
                        const transform = presented(transforms[rows], previous ~= nil and previous[index] or nil, alpha)
                        self.chunkKinds[rows] = chunk ~= nil
                        const tileSprite = chunk ~= nil and new rendercomponents.Sprite(
                            chunk.tileset,
                            0,
                            0,
                            1,
                            1
                        ) or nil
                        if chunk ~= nil then
                            run.tileBytes = tilechunk.packed(chunk)
                        end
                        self.clipIds[rows] = rowClips and rowClips[index].index or 0
                        if layers.isScreenSpace(transform.layer) then
                            run.screenSpace = true
                        end
                        const oldImage, oldSampler, oldLane, oldFlag = imageIds[
                            rows
                        ], samplers[rows], lanes[rows], castFlags[rows]
                        const tint = rowTints[index]
                        const depth = layers.depthOf(transform.layer, transform.z, transform.x, transform.y)
                        if entities[rows] ~= active.entities[index] or depths[rows] ~= depth then
                            orderChanged = true
                        end
                        entities[rows] = active.entities[index]
                        tints[rows] = tint
                        depths[rows] = depth
                        -- The lane is the tint's alpha and nothing else. The G-buffer
                        -- pass writes with replace and has nowhere to put partial
                        -- coverage, so an entity that is not fully opaque leaves for
                        -- the forward pass, where the depth it already sorted by
                        -- decides it against the opaque geometry in front of it.
                        const blended = tint.a < 1.0 or layers.isOverlay(transform.layer)
                        lanes[rows] = blended and LANE_BLEND or LANE_OPAQUE
                        -- A blended entity casts nothing: it never reaches the
                        -- G-buffer, so a hard silhouette of it would be a lie. An
                        -- entity carrying both cast components is an occluder, because
                        -- dropping that half would silently unblock a light.
                        local flag: integer = 0
                        local height: number = 0.0
                        if not blended then
                            if rowOccluders ~= nil then
                                flag = FLAG_OCCLUDER
                                height = rowOccluders[index].height
                            elseif rowDropShadows ~= nil then
                                flag = FLAG_DROP_SHADOW
                                height = rowDropShadows[index].height
                            end
                        end
                        castFlags[rows] = flag
                        castHeights[rows] = flag == 0 and 0.0 or height
                        if rowMaterials == nil then
                            materialIds[rows] = 0
                            params[rows] = 0.25
                        else
                            const material = rowMaterials[index]
                            if material.id < 0 or material.id >= materialCount then
                                error(
                                    "framepacket: material id " .. tostring(
                                        material.id
                                    ) .. " is not one this build carries",
                                    3
                                )
                            end
                            materialIds[rows] = material.id
                            params[rows] = material.param
                        end
                        if rowSprites == nil and tileSprite == nil then
                            imageIds[rows] = 0
                            samplers[rows] = 0
                            u0[rows] = 0.0
                            v0[rows] = 0.0
                            u1[rows] = 1.0
                            v1[rows] = 1.0
                        else
                            const sprite = tileSprite or assert(rowSprites)[index]
                            const image = sprite.image
                            -- An image that never became resident draws against the
                            -- backend's white fallback rather than dropping the entity.
                            if image ~= 0 and images.stateOf(image) == "resident" then
                                imageIds[rows] = image
                                samplers[rows] = images.samplerOf(image)
                            else
                                imageIds[rows] = 0
                                samplers[rows] = 0
                            end
                            u0[rows] = sprite.u0
                            v0[rows] = sprite.v0
                            u1[rows] = sprite.u1
                            v1[rows] = sprite.v1
                        end
                        if chunk ~= nil then
                            u0[
                                rows
                            ], v0[rows], u1[rows], v1[rows] = run.tileSlot, tilechunk.radius(chunk, transform), 0, 0
                        end
                        if oldImage ~= imageIds[
                            rows
                        ] or oldSampler ~= samplers[rows] or oldLane ~= lanes[rows] or oldFlag ~= castFlags[rows] then
                            self.batchDirty = true
                        end
                        ::nextTile::
                    end
                end
            end
        end
    end
    self.screenSpace = false
    for _, run in pairs(self.runs) do
        self.screenSpace = self.screenSpace or run.screenSpace
    end
    self.orderChanged = orderChanged or rows ~= self.rowCount
    self.rowCount = rows
end

--- Reads every light entity into the extractor's reused arrays.
--- @raises when a light holds a radius that is not greater than zero, or any
---     value that is not finite
local function collectLights(exclusive self: Extractor): nil
    const needed = self.lights:count()
    if needed > self.lightCapacity then
        const capacity = math.max(needed, self.lightCapacity * 2)
        self.lightTransforms = carray(rendercomponents.Transform2D, capacity + 1)
        self.lightValues = carray(lighting.PointLight2D, capacity + 1)
        self.lightCapacity = capacity
    end
    const lightEntities = self.lightEntities
    const lightTransforms = self.lightTransforms
    const lightValues = self.lightValues
    local _, _, alpha = self.world:getFixedTiming()
    local found: integer = 0
    unsafe do
        for candidate, count in self.lights:iter() do
            local active = candidate as archetype.Archetype
            local rowTransforms: rendercomponents.Transform2D[
                ?
            ] = assert(active:get(rendercomponents.Transform2DComponent))
            const previous = active:get(rendercomponents.PreviousTransform2DComponent)
            local rowLights: lighting.PointLight2D[?] = assert(active:get(lighting.PointLight2DComponent))
            for index = 1, count as integer do
                const light = rowLights[index]
                if not (light.radius > 0.0) or not finite(light.radius) then
                    error("framepacket: a PointLight2D radius must be greater than zero", 3)
                end
                if not finite(
                    light.height
                ) or not finite(
                    light.r
                ) or not finite(light.g) or not finite(light.b) or not finite(light.intensity) then
                    error("framepacket: a PointLight2D holds a value that is not finite", 3)
                end
                found = found + 1
                lightEntities[found] = active.entities[index]
                lightTransforms[found] = rowTransforms[index]
                presented(lightTransforms[found], previous ~= nil and previous[index] or nil, alpha)
                lightValues[found] = light
            end
        end
    end
    self.lightCount = found
end

--- Orders the collected lights by ascending entity id and applies the ceiling.
local function sortLights(exclusive self: Extractor): nil
    const order = self.lightOrder
    const found = self.lightCount
    for index = 1, found do
        order[index] = index
    end
    for index = found + 1, self.lightsSorted do
        order[index] = nil
    end
    self.lightsSorted = found
    table.sort(order, self.beforeLight)
    if found > lighting.MAX_LIGHTS then
        self.lightCount = lighting.MAX_LIGHTS
    end
end

--- Orders the collected rows farthest first, breaking ties by entity id.
local function sortRows(exclusive self: Extractor): nil
    if not self.orderChanged then
        return
    end
    const order = self.order
    const rows = self.rowCount
    for index = 1, rows do
        order[index] = index
    end
    for index = rows + 1, self.sorted do
        order[index] = nil
    end
    self.sorted = rows
    table.sort(order, self.before)
    self.orderChanged = false
end

local watched: {
    tecs.internal.components.Component
} = {
    rendercomponents.Transform2DComponent,
    rendercomponents.TintComponent,
    rendercomponents.PreviousTransform2DComponent,
    rendercomponents.SpriteComponent,
    materials.MaterialComponent,
    lighting.Occluder2DComponent,
    lighting.DropShadow2DComponent,
    clips.ClipComponent,
    tilechunk.TileChunkComponent,
}

-- Port of SpriteExtractor.layoutPacked and its clean-run gate. Length or
-- offset changes relayout the packed scene; otherwise only dirty runs rewrite.
-- Monotonic write counts preserve changes across end-of-frame dirty clears.
local function sceneChanged(exclusive self: Extractor, eye: View, snapshot: boolean): boolean
    local force = not self.cacheValid or snapshot
    const layerVersion, clipVersion = layers.revision(), clips.revision()
    const imageVersion, materialVersion = images.residencyRevision(), materials.revision()
    force = force
        or layerVersion ~= self.cachedLayers
        or clipVersion ~= self.cachedClips
        or imageVersion ~= self.cachedImages
        or materialVersion ~= self.cachedMaterials
    const viewport = {eye.width, eye.height, eye.x, eye.y, eye.zoom, eye.rotation}
    if self.screenSpace then
        for index, value in ipairs(viewport) do
            force = force or self.cachedView[index] ~= value
        end
    end
    for _, run in pairs(self.runs) do
        run.seen = false
    end
    local total: integer = 0
    local tileSlot: integer = 0
    local relayout = not self.cacheValid
    local changed = force
    local _, _, alpha = self.world:getFixedTiming()
    unsafe do
        for candidate, first, last, runKey in sources(self) do
            const active = candidate as archetype.Archetype
            const count = assert(last) - assert(first) + 1
            local run = self.runs[assert(runKey)]
            if run == nil or run.archetype ~= active then
                run = new Run(
                    archetype = active,
                    offset = total,
                    length = count as integer,
                    structAt = -1,
                    valueAt = {},
                    dirty = true,
                    seen = true,
                    screenSpace = false,
                    signature = ""
                )
                self.runs[assert(runKey)] = run
                relayout = true
            end
            const structural = active:structuralCount()
            run.dirty = force or run.structAt ~= structural or (
                alpha ~= self.cachedAlpha and active:get(rendercomponents.PreviousTransform2DComponent) ~= nil
            )
            run.structAt = structural
            for index, component in ipairs(watched) do
                const writes = active:writeCount(component)
                run.dirty = run.dirty or run.valueAt[index] ~= writes
                run.valueAt[index] = writes
            end
            const chunks = active:get(tilechunk.TileChunkComponent)
            if run.dirty and chunks ~= nil then
                local parts: {string} = {}
                for _, component in ipairs(watched) do
                    -- Every watched drawable component has native struct storage.
                    const column = active:get(component) as any
                    if column ~= nil then
                        const item = column[assert(first)]
                        parts[#parts + 1] = ffi.string(ffi.cast("const char *", item), ffi.sizeof(item))
                    end
                end
                const signature = table.concat(parts)
                run.dirty = force or run.signature ~= signature or (
                    alpha ~= self.cachedAlpha and active:get(rendercomponents.PreviousTransform2DComponent) ~= nil
                )
                run.signature = signature
            end
            local length = run.length
            if run.dirty then
                length = count as integer
                if chunks ~= nil then
                    length = 0
                    for index = assert(first), assert(last) do
                        length = length + (tilechunk.count(chunks[index]) > 0 and 1 or 0)
                    end
                end
            end
            if chunks ~= nil and length > 0 then
                relayout = relayout or run.tileSlot ~= tileSlot
                run.tileSlot = tileSlot
                tileSlot = tileSlot + 1
            end
            relayout = relayout or run.offset ~= total or run.length ~= length
            run.offset, run.length, run.seen = total, length, true
            total = total + length
            changed = changed or run.dirty
        end
    end
    for id, run in pairs(self.runs) do
        if not run.seen then
            self.runs[id] = nil
            relayout = true
        end
    end
    self.relayout = relayout
    self.batchDirty = relayout
    self.rewritten = 0
    for _, run in pairs(self.runs) do
        run.dirty = run.dirty or relayout
        if run.dirty then
            self.rewritten = self.rewritten + run.length
        end
    end
    self.cachedView, self.cachedAlpha = viewport, alpha
    self.cachedLayers, self.cachedClips = layerVersion, clipVersion
    self.cachedImages, self.cachedMaterials = imageVersion, materialVersion

    return changed or relayout
end

local function rebuildBatches(exclusive self: Extractor): nil
    const order, rows = self.order, self.rowCount
    const imageIds, samplers, lanes = self.imageIds, self.samplers, self.lanes
    local runImage: integer = -1
    local runSampler: integer = -1
    local runChunk = false
    local runLane: integer = -1
    local batchBuffer = nupp.io.newBuffer()
    local batchWriter = nupp.io.newScalarWriter(batchBuffer)
    runImage = -1
    runSampler = -1
    runLane = -1
    local runFirst: integer = 0
    local runLength: integer = 0
    for index = 1, rows do
        const row = order[index]
        if imageIds[
            row
        ] ~= runImage or samplers[row] ~= runSampler or lanes[row] ~= runLane or self.chunkKinds[row] ~= runChunk then
            if runLength > 0 then
                batchWriter:writeUint32(wrap(runImage))
                    :writeUint32(wrap(runSampler))
                    :writeUint32(wrap(runLane))
                    :writeUint32(wrap(runFirst))
                    :writeUint32(wrap(runLength))
            end
            runChunk = self.chunkKinds[row]
            runImage = imageIds[row]
            runSampler = samplers[row]
            runLane = lanes[row]
            runFirst = index - 1
            runLength = 0
        end
        runLength = runLength + 1
    end
    if runLength > 0 then
        batchWriter:writeUint32(wrap(runImage))
            :writeUint32(wrap(runSampler))
            :writeUint32(wrap(runLane))
            :writeUint32(wrap(runFirst))
            :writeUint32(wrap(runLength))
    end

    batchWriter:drop()
    self.cachedBatchBytes = batchBuffer:getString()
    batchBuffer:drop()
    self.cachedBatches = #self.cachedBatchBytes // 20
    local casters: integer = 0
    for index = 1, rows do
        if self.castFlags[index] ~= 0 then
            casters = casters + 1
        end
    end
    self.cachedCasters = casters
end

local function prefix(exclusive self: Extractor, eye: View, mode: integer, revision: integer): string
    const batches, rows, casters = self.cachedBatches, self.rowCount, self.cachedCasters
    const shadowTuning = lighting.shadows()
    const bloomTuning = lighting.bloom()
    -- A frame with no caster and no light runs the shadow lane over an empty
    -- list, so the flag is the tuning alone and the backend does not have to
    -- learn a second reason a pass might be skipped.
    local frameFlags: integer = 0
    if shadowTuning ~= nil then
        frameFlags = frameFlags + FRAME_SHADOWS
    end
    if bloomTuning ~= nil then
        frameFlags = frameFlags + FRAME_BLOOM
    end
    frameFlags = frameFlags + mode
    const ambientR, ambientG, ambientB = lighting.ambient()
    const lightCount = self.lightCount

    local tileUpdates: {string} = {}
    if mode ~= FRAME_RETAINED then
        for _, run in pairs(self.runs) do
            if run.length > 0 and run.tileBytes ~= "" and (mode == 0 or run.dirty) then
                local tileBuffer = nupp.io.newBuffer()
                local tileWriter = nupp.io.newScalarWriter(tileBuffer)
                tileWriter:writeUint32(wrap(run.tileSlot)):writeBytes(run.tileBytes)
                tileWriter:drop()
                tileUpdates[#tileUpdates + 1] = tileBuffer:getString()
                tileBuffer:drop()
            end
        end
    end
    const graph = passes.section()
    local buffer = nupp.io.newBuffer()
    local writer = nupp.io.newScalarWriter(buffer)
    writer:writeUint32(MAGIC)
        :writeUint32(VERSION)
        :writeUint32(HEADER_SIZE)
        :writeUint32(wrap(frameFlags))
        :writeUint32(wrap(passes.revision()))
        :writeUint32(wrap(#graph))
        :writeUint32(BATCH_STRIDE)
        :writeUint32(wrap(batches))
        :writeUint32(INSTANCE_STRIDE)
        :writeUint32(wrap(rows))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(eye.width))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(eye.height))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(eye.x))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(eye.y))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(eye.zoom))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(eye.rotation))
        :writeUint32(LIGHT_STRIDE)
        :writeUint32(wrap(lightCount))
        :writeUint32(wrap(casters))
        :writeUint32(wrap(revision))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(ambientR))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(ambientG))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(ambientB))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(shadowTuning ~= nil and shadowTuning.steps or 24.0))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(shadowTuning ~= nil and shadowTuning.height or 64.0))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(shadowTuning ~= nil and shadowTuning.margin or 200.0))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(shadowTuning ~= nil and shadowTuning.dropOpacity or 0.4))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(shadowTuning ~= nil and shadowTuning.dropLength or 512.0))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(bloomTuning ~= nil and bloomTuning.threshold or 0.8))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(bloomTuning ~= nil and bloomTuning.knee or 0.1))
        :writeFloat32(narrow(bloomTuning ~= nil and bloomTuning.intensity or 0.7))
        :writeUint32(wrap(#tileUpdates))
    writer:writeBytes(graph)

    const lightOrder = self.lightOrder
    const lightTransforms = self.lightTransforms
    const lightValues = self.lightValues
    unsafe do
        for index = 1, lightCount do
            const slot = lightOrder[index]
            const transform = lightTransforms[slot]
            const light = lightValues[slot]
            writer:writeFloat32(narrow(transform.x))
                :writeFloat32(narrow(transform.y))
                :writeFloat32(narrow(light.height))
                :writeFloat32(narrow(light.radius))
                :writeFloat32(narrow(light.r))
                :writeFloat32(narrow(light.g))
                :writeFloat32(narrow(light.b))
                :writeFloat32(narrow(light.intensity))
        end
    end

    writer:writeBytes(table.concat(tileUpdates))
    if mode == 0 then
        writer:writeBytes(self.cachedBatchBytes)
    end
    writer:drop()
    const bytes = buffer:getString()
    buffer:drop()

    return bytes
end

local function packInstances(exclusive self: Extractor, eye: View, full: boolean): nil
    const lanes, castFlags = self.lanes, self.castFlags
    const depths = self.depths
    const transforms = self.transforms
    const tints = self.tints
    const castHeights = self.castHeights
    const materialIds = self.materialIds
    const params = self.params
    const u0 = self.u0
    const v0 = self.v0
    const u1 = self.u1
    const v1 = self.v1
    const cameraX, cameraY, zoom, rotation = eye.x, eye.y, eye.zoom, eye.rotation
    const width, height = eye.width, eye.height
    const wordsNeeded = self.rowCount * 20
    if self.instanceWords.count < wordsNeeded then
        local capacity = self.instanceWords.count
        while capacity < wordsNeeded do
            capacity = capacity * 2
        end
        self.instanceWords = array.scalar(array.uint32, capacity)
    end
    self.ranges:clear()
    local output = self.instanceWords:write()
    do
        local pointer, length = output:ref()
        assert(wordsNeeded <= length)
        unsafe do
            local raw = (pointer as uint32*) + 0
            local floats = borrowFrom(ffi.cast<float[?]>(raw), output)
            local words = borrowFrom(ffi.cast<uint32[?]>(raw), output)
            for _, run in pairs(self.runs) do
                if full or run.dirty then
                    local low: integer = self.rowCount
                    local high: integer = 0
                    for row = run.offset + 1, run.offset + run.length do
                        const index = self.drawSlots[row]
                        low, high = math.min(low, index - 1) as integer, math.max(high, index) as integer
                        const transform = transforms[row]
                        const tint = tints[row]
                        const base = (index - 1) * 20
                        local x, y, angle, sx, sy = transform.x, transform.y, transform.rotation, transform.scaleX, transform.scaleY
                        if layers.isScreenSpace(transform.layer) then
                            -- Express target-pixel geometry in the common camera's
                            -- world space. Culling and drawing then agree without a
                            -- second rendering path.
                            local dx, dy = (x - width * 0.5) / zoom, (y - height * 0.5) / zoom
                            local c, s = math.cos(rotation), math.sin(rotation)
                            x, y = cameraX + dx * c - dy * s, cameraY + dx * s + dy * c
                            angle, sx, sy = angle + rotation, sx / zoom, sy / zoom
                        end
                        floats[base + 0] = x as float
                        floats[base + 1] = y as float
                        floats[base + 2] = angle as float
                        floats[base + 3] = depths[row] as float
                        floats[base + 4] = sx as float
                        floats[base + 5] = sy as float
                        floats[base + 6] = params[row] as float
                        floats[base + 7] = castHeights[row] as float
                        floats[base + 8] = u0[row] as float
                        floats[
                            base + 9
                        ] = (
                            self.chunkKinds[row] and layers.isScreenSpace(transform.layer) and v0[row] / zoom or v0[row]
                        ) as float
                        floats[base + 10] = u1[row] as float
                        floats[base + 11] = v1[row] as float
                        floats[base + 12] = tint.r as float
                        floats[base + 13] = tint.g as float
                        floats[base + 14] = tint.b as float
                        floats[base + 15] = tint.a as float
                        words[base + 16] = wrap(materialIds[row])
                        local flag = (
                            lanes[row] == LANE_BLEND and FLAG_BLENDED or 0
                        ) + castFlags[row] + (self.chunkKinds[row] and 16 or 0)
                        local leftTop, rightBottom = 0, 0
                        if self.clipIds[row] ~= 0 then
                            local left, top, right, bottom = clips.regionOf(self.clipIds[row])
                            -- Pixel centers are half-integers. Quantizing at that
                            -- boundary preserves exact coverage in the single-sample
                            -- renderer.
                            left = math.max(0, math.min(65535, math.ceil(left - 0.5)))
                            top = math.max(0, math.min(65535, math.ceil(top - 0.5)))
                            right = math.max(0, math.min(65535, math.ceil(right - 0.5)))
                            bottom = math.max(0, math.min(65535, math.ceil(bottom - 0.5)))
                            leftTop, rightBottom = left + top * 65536, right + bottom * 65536
                            flag = flag + FLAG_CLIPPED
                        end
                        words[base + 17] = wrap(flag)
                        words[base + 18] = wrap(leftTop as integer)
                        words[base + 19] = wrap(rightBottom as integer)
                    end
                    self.ranges:mark(low * 80, (high - low) * 80)
                end
            end
        end
    end
    output:drop()
    self.ranges:sort()
end

local function payload(exclusive self: Extractor, delta: boolean, baseRevision: integer): string
    local pieces: {string} = {}
    if delta then
        local buffer = nupp.io.newBuffer()
        local writer = nupp.io.newScalarWriter(buffer)
        writer:writeUint32(wrap(baseRevision)):writeUint32(wrap(self.ranges.count))
        for index = 0, self.ranges.count - 1 do
            const offset, size = self.ranges:at(index)
            writer:writeUint32(wrap(offset)):writeUint32(wrap(size))
        end
        writer:drop()
        pieces[1] = buffer:getString()
        buffer:drop()
    end
    local input = self.instanceWords:read()
    do
        local pointer, length = input:ref()
        assert(self.rowCount * 20 <= length)
        unsafe do
            local raw = (pointer as uint8*) + 0
            local bytes = borrowFrom(ffi.cast<uint8*>(raw), input)
            if delta then
                for index = 0, self.ranges.count - 1 do
                    const offset, size = self.ranges:at(index)
                    pieces[#pieces + 1] = ffi.string(bytes + offset, size)
                end
            else
                pieces[1] = ffi.string(bytes, self.rowCount * 80)
            end
        end
    end

    return table.concat(pieces)
end

local function encode(exclusive self: Extractor, width: integer, height: integer, residentRevision: integer?): string
    assert(width > 0 and height > 0, "framepacket: viewport dimensions must be positive")
    const cameraX, cameraY, zoom, rotation = view(self, width, height)
    const eye = new View(width = width, height = height, x = cameraX, y = cameraY, zoom = zoom, rotation = rotation)
    const previous = self.sceneRevision
    const matched = self.cacheValid and residentRevision ~= nil and residentRevision == previous
    const changed = sceneChanged(self, eye, residentRevision == nil)
    self.cacheValid = false
    local reordered = false
    if changed then
        self.sceneRevision = self.sceneRevision + 1
        assert(self.sceneRevision <= 4294967295, "framepacket: scene revision exhausted")
        zone.push("extract/collect")
        collect(self)
        zone.pop()
        reordered = self.orderChanged
        if reordered then
            zone.push("extract/sort")
            sortRows(self)
            for index, row in ipairs(self.order) do
                self.drawSlots[row] = index
            end
            zone.pop()
        end
    end
    const layoutChanged = self.batchDirty or reordered
    if layoutChanged then
        rebuildBatches(self)
    end
    zone.push("extract/lights")
    collectLights(self)
    sortLights(self)
    zone.pop()
    local mode: integer = 0
    if matched and not changed then
        mode = FRAME_RETAINED
    elseif matched and not layoutChanged and not self.relayout and self.rewritten < self.rowCount then
        mode = FRAME_DELTA
    end
    zone.push("extract/encode")
    const head = prefix(self, eye, mode, residentRevision ~= nil and self.sceneRevision or 0)
    local bytes = head
    if mode ~= FRAME_RETAINED then
        packInstances(self, eye, mode ~= FRAME_DELTA)
        bytes = head .. payload(self, mode == FRAME_DELTA, previous)
    end
    self.cacheValid = residentRevision ~= nil
    zone.pop()

    return bytes
end

function Extractor.packet(exclusive self: Extractor, width: integer, height: integer): string
    return encode(self, width, height, nil)
end

function Extractor.frame(exclusive self: Extractor, width: integer, height: integer, residentRevision: integer): string
    return encode(self, width, height, residentRevision)
end
